$0:KERNEL
$0:format{cortex:1.0,encoding:UTF-8,language:en}
$0:enum_phase{values:"P0|P1|P2|P3|P4|P5"}
$0:enum_sev{values:"blocking|high|medium|low"}
RUL:rule{type:attrs,weight:H,focus:rule,desc:"Normative rule",fields:"rule:text|detail:text"}
CMD:cmd{type:attrs,weight:H,focus:command,desc:"Executable step",fields:"command:text|expect:text"}
FIX:fix{type:attrs,weight:H,focus:issue,desc:"Adjustment item; sev is blocking, high, medium or low",fields:"issue:text|action:text|accept:text|evidence:text|sev:atom"}
GATE:gate{type:attrs,weight:H,focus:criterion,desc:"Gate",fields:"criterion:text|evidence:text"}
MET:metric{type:attrs,weight:H,focus:definition,desc:"Metric",fields:"definition:text|unit:atom|formula:text?"}
RSK:risk{type:attrs,weight:M,focus:threat,desc:"Threat",fields:"threat:text|control:text"}
PRC:step{type:attrs-pos,weight:H,focus:action,desc:"Procedure step",pos:"action:text|expect:text|phase:atom"}
ART:artifact{type:attrs,weight:M,focus:path,desc:"Artifact",fields:"path:text|content:text"}
TMPL:template{type:bloque,weight:M,desc:"Template"}
TXT:note{type:cuerpo,weight:M,desc:"Rationale"}
$1: MISSION:CORE
TXT:mission{
Remediation and completion package for the CODEC-CORTEX 1.0.1 benchmark.
An autonomous agent reads this canonical CORTEX document and executes the fixes,
completes the untested model phases, and hardens operations until every acceptance
criterion is met with sealed, durable, hash-traceable evidence. Author in canonical
CORTEX; render HCORTEX only via the toolchain; never hand-write HCORTEX layout.
}
RUL:objective{rule:"Achieve 100% of the pre-registered acceptance criteria: all gates G1-G6 green, zero silent content loss, zero dropped failures, every claim hash-traceable, reproducible offline.",detail:"100% is a verifiable checklist target, not an absolute promise of model performance or a general claim that CORTEX is better. No claim without a metric, interval, conditions, artifact and hash."}
RUL:autonomy{rule:"The agent may choose models, questions and corpus only during pre-registration, never after seeing results. Freeze order: prereg -> runs -> analysis -> report.",detail:"A new question or a changed expectation is a NEW run with a new preregistration; never rename or relax a hypothesis post-hoc. Exploratory metrics must be labeled exploratory."}
RUL:owner_control{rule:"The owner approves before: any model spend (cost cap), publishing results, opening upstream PRs, and any destructive or irreversible operation.",detail:"Credentials are always owner-provided in the connection config; never embed secrets in sealed artifacts or reports; exclude secrets from the seal. The agent acts with maximum autonomy inside these gates."}
RUL:safety{rule:"Use an allowlist of commands; isolated venv; pinned versions; no network during measurement; bounded logs; explicit loop exit conditions.",detail:"Never run an infinite unbounded console loop. Tee full logs to a rotated file; print only summaries/heartbeats to console (e.g., Jenkins)."}
RUL:evidence{rule:"Every claim line carries metric, estimate, CI, n, artifact path and sha256. The seal must verify. Negative results get the same prominence as confirmed ones.",detail:"A benchmark that cannot fail is marketing. Report failed attempts in the denominator; never drop them silently."}
$2: BASELINE:DATA
TXT:baseline{
Starting state from run 20261115T000000Z-cortex101-p1 (deterministic phase, sealed, 229 files, seal PASS).
H1 fidelity CONFIRMED 1.000 [0.862,1.000] n=24.
H2 determinism CONFIRMED 1.000 [0.862,1.000] n=24 R=5.
H3 density CONFIRMED median paired diff cortex-json -20.094 [-60.091,-19.432] tokens/fact; cortex 11.945 vs json 32.084; pre-BPE proxy tokenizer.
H4 comprehension UNTESTED. H5 generation UNTESTED (no declared model API).
H6 error precision FALSIFIED 0.727 [0.434,0.903] n=11 (B08->G015, B09->L010, B11->S003).
H7 tamper file-sha256 CONFIRMED 1.000; canonical-hash FALSIFIED 0.979 (94/96; formatting-only tamper invisible to AST hash by design).
Silent-acceptance DEFECT: 3/4 non-canonical layouts accepted with 0 diagnostics and total content loss (as-received package compiled to 0/70 ideas).
Conformance DEFECT: wheel ships no corpus; verdict error, total 0.
prereg sha256 974bd7b13519a667a30286a72b0fb091d266772f5450d49c854594277468e6e6.
corpus seal sha256 281cd7005951bf47f327845f2343f22985d4ef932499cf8f3c9c345063e2c724.
report.md sha256 a1d757a14a8fc4823a930bd40b2233593014b4f9970e2255472a1d9914905c9b.
}
ART:baseline_run{path:"runs/20261115T000000Z-cortex101-p1",content:"manifest.json, prereg.yaml, corpus/, baselines/, metrics/, stats.json, report.md, SHA256SUMS, tools/repro_p1.py"}
$3: FIXES_TOOLCHAIN:CORE
FIX:f01_silent_acceptance{issue:"HCORTEX 1.0.1 compiler accepts non-canonical layouts and silently drops ALL content with zero diagnostics; loss-report still says reversible=true (as-received package -> 0/70 ideas).",action:"Implement a precompile guard validator (layout + content coverage); require a specific diagnostic for any unrecognized non-whitespace content inside schema blocks; file an upstream issue with repro vectors C01-C04. Never trust compile success alone.",accept:"silent_acceptance_rate=0 on C-vectors; coverage=1.0 or declared losses for every accepted document; upstream issue filed with sealed repro hashes.",evidence:"metrics/silent_audit.json + guard report + upstream issue link",sev:blocking}
FIX:f02_loss_report_scope{issue:"loss-report measures only the render direction of what was parsed; it reports reversible=true even after compile-side content loss.",action:"Add compile-side coverage accounting: source ideas/facts vs compiled ideas/facts; the guard computes coverage; gate on loss-report AND coverage jointly. Upstream: loss-report should include compile losses.",accept:"coverage metric computed for every document; a clean loss-report with coverage<1.0 is treated as a defect, not a pass.",evidence:"metrics/coverage.json + guard report",sev:blocking}
FIX:f03_conformance_packaging{issue:"python -m codec_cortex conformance returns verdict error, total 0 because the wheel ships no conformance/slots corpus.",action:"Upstream: include the conformance corpus in the wheel/sdist. Interim: build a local manifest from the sealed corpus and run the harness against it (declared deviation, not the shipped-corpus claim).",accept:"conformance runs with total>0 and zero failures on the local sealed corpus; upstream issue filed; deviation documented in report.",evidence:"metrics/conformance.txt + local manifest",sev:high}
FIX:f04_error_precision{issue:"H6 falsified 0.727: B08 emitted G015 (expected S005), B09 emitted L010 (expected S006), B11 emitted S003 (expected L001); L010 was absent from the scanned catalog.",action:"Audit catalog completeness (document every emitted code). Then EITHER fix parser precedence upstream OR open a NEW preregistration with corrected frozen vector expectations. Never rename H6 post-hoc.",accept:"new run error_code_precision=1.0 on frozen vectors; catalog documents all emitted codes; both the original falsified result and the new result are reported.",evidence:"metrics/errors.json + new prereg.yaml + catalog audit",sev:high}
FIX:f05_dual_hash_audit{issue:"Canonical hash is AST-level: 2/96 one-byte formatting tampers were invisible to it (by design). File-level sha256 detected 96/96.",action:"Seal FILE bytes (SHA256SUMS) as the primary audit channel; record canonical hash as secondary in the manifest; document AST-level semantics so consumers do not over-trust the canonical hash.",accept:"tamper_detection(file)=1.0; canonical-channel expectation explicitly declared in prereg; manifest carries both hashes per artifact.",evidence:"SHA256SUMS + manifest.json + report threats section",sev:medium}
$4: FIXES_ARTIFACTS:CORE
FIX:f06_canonical_by_render{issue:"The as-received .hcortex.md is non-canonical for 1.0.1 (bare section heads, no blank line before schema marker, vertical-cell tables, idea heads without ###).",action:"Never hand-write HCORTEX. Author canonical CORTEX and render via to-hcortex so layout is canonical by construction. Keep the as-received file only as an adversarial vector. Normalize existing sources via declared transforms T1/T2/T3/T3b.",accept:"every distributed .hcortex.md is renderer output; roundtrip equals source canonical form; as-received preserved as a labeled vector.",evidence:"corpus/index.json + metrics/fidelity.json",sev:blocking}
FIX:f07_guard_validator{issue:"No precompile lint exists to catch layout deviations and content loss before trusting the toolchain.",action:"Implement tools/guard.py: check section layout (## section head + blank line + schema open/close), ### idea heads, single-row Markdown tables, fenced bloque bodies, no column-0 braces inside bodies, ASCII identifiers; compute idea/fact coverage source vs compiled; emit specific codes on deviation.",accept:"guard rejects C01-C04 with specific codes and passes all valid A-docs; coverage=1.0 on A; guard is a blocking gate before any compile result is trusted.",evidence:"tools/guard.py + guard report + metrics/coverage.json",sev:blocking}
FIX:f08_sealing_protocol{issue:"Ephemeral sandbox resets destroyed run directories during execution; a sealed run must survive beyond the sandbox.",action:"Persist the run directory to owner-controlled durable storage (git commit or tar export) BEFORE publishing; seal then export; re-verify the seal on the durable copy after extract.",accept:"sealed run survives a sandbox reset; sha256sum -c passes on the durable copy; export hash recorded.",evidence:"durable run copy + seal verify log + export sha256",sev:high}
$5: FIXES_BENCHMARK:FLOW
FIX:f09_model_phases{issue:"H4 comprehension and H5 generation are UNTESTED; no model-facing benefit is established.",action:"Open a NEW preregistration: >=2 declared model ids and dates (include small models for long-horizon agentic use), 6 formats x 8 questions x R=5, identical prompts verbatim, fixed temperature/top_p, deterministic rubric frozen before runs, one JSON cell per attempt, no silent retries, failures counted in the denominator. If an LLM judge is used, validate it against a human sample and report agreement.",accept:"planned cells = completed + failed; H4/H5 verdicts with paired CIs and Holm correction; cost per cell recorded; raw outputs stored before scoring.",evidence:"cells/ + scores/ + stats.json + prereg.yaml",sev:high}
FIX:f10_real_bpe{issue:"Density H3 used a pre-BPE proxy tokenizer (cl100k-pretoken-v1); real BPE merges may favor JSON.",action:"Open a NEW preregistration H3b with a real declared tokenizer (e.g., tiktoken cl100k_base and o200k_base for contrast), pre-cached for offline measurement; rerun density; report proxy and real side by side; never mutate the old run.",accept:"H3b verdict with real-BPE CIs; tokenizer id and version in manifest; both runs preserved and sealed.",evidence:"metrics/density_bpe.json + new prereg.yaml",sev:high}
FIX:f11_stats_reporting{issue:"Ensure the analysis uses only pre-registered statistics and full reporting.",action:"Wilson intervals for rates; paired bootstrap CI of median paired difference; two-sided sign test; Holm correction over the family of p-values; effect sizes; per-repetition data (R=5 not treated as 5 independent questions); n attempted/completed/failed per cell; report follows the 10-section skeleton.",accept:"stats.json cites the hypothesis id per test; report claim table complete with path+sha256 per line.",evidence:"stats.json + report.md",sev:medium}
FIX:f12_validity_controls{issue:"Contamination, format familiarity, prompt bias and tokenizer shift threaten validity.",action:"Use held-out and zero-shot unfamiliar corpora with provenance and dates; equal information and equal instruction budget across formats; identical prompts and fixed order plus a small prompt-robustness check; declare the tokenizer; state JSON/Markdown familiarity as a limitation, not hidden.",accept:"controls applied and documented in the threats section; asymmetry disclosed; no absolute claims.",evidence:"report.md threats section + corpus provenance",sev:medium}
$6: FIXES_OPS:FLOW
FIX:f13_durable_env{issue:"Sandbox ephemerality and version drift undermine reproducibility.",action:"Isolated venv; pin codec-cortex==1.0.1 and dependencies; record OS, CPU, Python, pip and package versions/hashes in manifest.json; no network during measurement; durable storage for sealed runs; single-command offline repro from the sealed corpus.",accept:"manifest complete; third party reproduces P1 offline from the sealed corpus without any model call.",evidence:"manifest.json + tools/repro_p1.py",sev:high}
FIX:f14_bounded_logs{issue:"Agentic loops (e.g., Jenkins) can grow console logs without bound and run forever.",action:"Tee full logs to a rotated file with a max size; console prints only summaries/heartbeats; define explicit loop exit conditions and a max iteration count; never an infinite unbounded console loop.",accept:"log size bounded and rotated; loop terminates deterministically; CI console stays readable.",evidence:"CI config + log rotation policy + exit-condition spec",sev:medium}
FIX:f15_credentials_owner{issue:"Model API authentication and secret handling.",action:"Use owner-provided credentials in the connection config; never embed secrets in sealed artifacts or reports; exclude secrets from the seal; run a secret scan before publish; owner approves a cost cap before any model spend.",accept:"no secret present in any sealed file; cost cap enforced and logged; approval recorded.",evidence:"secret scan report + approval record",sev:blocking}
FIX:f16_economics{issue:"Quantify personal/professional ROI of the ultra-dense context pattern without overclaiming.",action:"Record MET:cost per cell; compute cost-per-fact and projected token savings for agentic loops (density ratio x token price); include a small-model long-horizon drift check; label the savings estimate exploratory until H4/H5 confirm no accuracy loss; state model, corpus, prompt and tokenizer conditions.",accept:"cost table and savings estimate with CIs and explicit conditions; no absolute claim; exploratory label until model phases confirm.",evidence:"metrics/cost.json + report economics section",sev:medium}
$7: PROTOCOL:FLOW
PRC:p0_setup|"Install the pinned package in an isolated venv; record manifest.json; run selfcheck and the guard."|"G1: manifest and prereg hashes recorded"|P0
PRC:p1_freeze|"Build/normalize corpus, baselines and vectors; write prereg.yaml; seal; record hashes in manifest."|"prereg and corpus seals present in manifest"|P0
PRC:p2_guard|"Run the guard validator on every source; compute coverage; reject silent loss before trusting compile."|"coverage=1.0 or declared losses; silent_acceptance_rate=0"|P1
PRC:p3_deterministic|"Run fidelity, determinism R=5, density with real BPE, error precision, tamper and latency offline."|"P1 metrics for every corpus document, none missing"|P1
PRC:p4_models|"After owner cost approval, run H4/H5 cells R=5; store raw output before scoring; count failures."|"planned = completed + failed; cells sealed"|P2
PRC:p5_analysis|"Compute only pre-registered statistics: Wilson, paired bootstrap, sign test, Holm."|"stats.json cites the hypothesis id per test"|P4
PRC:p6_report_seal|"Write the 10-section report and claim table with hashes; seal; export to durable storage; verify the seal."|"G5: seal verifies and every claim is traceable"|P4
PRC:p7_upstream|"File upstream issues (silent acceptance, conformance packaging, error catalog) with sealed repro vectors; owner approves any PR."|"issues filed with hashes; no unapproved publishing"|P5
$8: COMMANDS:CORE
CMD:install{command:"python -m pip install codec-cortex==1.0.1",expect:"import succeeds and codec_cortex.__version__ is 1.0.1"}
CMD:verify_hash{command:"python -m codec_cortex hash <file.cortex>",expect:"prints sha256:64hex; identical across repeated runs (canonical/AST-level hash)"}
CMD:guard{command:"python tools/guard.py <run-dir>",expect:"coverage=1.0; silent_acceptance_rate=0; specific codes on C-vectors"}
CMD:selfcheck{command:"python -m codec_cortex loss-report <file.cortex>",expect:"reversible true and losses empty AND guard coverage=1.0; otherwise STOP and report a defect"}
CMD:render{command:"python -m codec_cortex to-hcortex <file.cortex>",expect:"deterministic canonical HCORTEX; same bytes on every run"}
CMD:compile{command:"python -m codec_cortex from-hcortex <file.hcortex.md>",expect:"canonical CORTEX; roundtrip equals the source canonical form"}
CMD:conformance_local{command:"python -m codec_cortex conformance <local-manifest-dir>",expect:"total>0 and zero failures on the local sealed corpus (declared deviation)"}
CMD:repro{command:"python tools/repro_p1.py <run-dir>",expect:"recomputes P1 rates from the sealed corpus; no model call; no network"}
CMD:seal_verify{command:"sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS",expect:"all files OK; 0 mismatches"}
CMD:export{command:"tar czf run.tar.gz <run-dir> && sha256sum run.tar.gz",expect:"durable copy created; seal verifies after extract; export hash recorded"}
$9: GATES:CORE
GATE:g1{criterion:"Pre-registration frozen before any model call; hashes in manifest.",evidence:"prereg sha256 committed before the first cell"}
GATE:g2{criterion:"Deterministic phase complete with results or declared defects.",evidence:"P1 metrics for every corpus document, none missing"}
GATE:g3{criterion:"Every planned cell accounted for as completed or failed.",evidence:"counts per cell match the matrix; failures reported as failures"}
GATE:g4{criterion:"Analysis uses only pre-registered tests and corrections.",evidence:"stats.json cites the hypothesis id per test"}
GATE:g5{criterion:"Every claim cites artifact path and sha256; the seal verifies.",evidence:"sha256sum -c passes; claim table complete"}
GATE:g6{criterion:"Zero silent loss; coverage=1.0 or declared; guard rejects non-canonical layout.",evidence:"guard report + metrics/coverage.json"}
$10: METRICS:CORE
MET:coverage{definition:"Share of source ideas/facts preserved through compile plus guard.",unit:ratio,formula:"preserved / source"}
MET:silent_acceptance_rate{definition:"Share of non-canonical vectors accepted with zero diagnostics and content loss.",unit:ratio,formula:"silent / vectors"}
MET:cost{definition:"Total model tokens consumed per cell including prompt and completion; basis for cost-per-fact and savings.",unit:tokens,formula:"sum(prompt, completion)"}
TXT:metrics_ref{
fidelity_rate, byte_determinism, token_density, answer_accuracy, generation_validity,
error_code_precision, tamper_detection and latency are defined exactly as in the baseline
benchmark package and are reused unchanged. New metrics here are coverage,
silent_acceptance_rate and cost.
}
$11: RISKS:CORE
RSK:silent_loss{threat:"Toolchain reports a clean self-check while truncating content.",control:"Guard plus coverage gate G6; never trust loss-report alone; require coverage=1.0 or declared losses."}
RSK:ephemeral{threat:"Sandbox resets destroy run directories.",control:"Durable export plus seal verification; commit before publishing; record export hash."}
RSK:cost_runaway{threat:"Model loops overspend or run forever.",control:"Owner cost cap; bounded iterations; explicit exit conditions; approval gate before spend."}
RSK:log_flood{threat:"Infinite loop floods the CI console.",control:"Rotated file logs; console summaries only; max log size; deterministic termination."}
RSK:secret_leak{threat:"Credentials get sealed or published.",control:"Owner-provided credentials; secret scan before publish; exclude secrets from the seal."}
RSK:posthoc{threat:"Tuning hypotheses or vectors after seeing results.",control:"Freeze before runs; a new question is a new run; label exploratory metrics."}
RSK:tokenizer_shift{threat:"Density conclusions shift with the tokenizer.",control:"Declare a real BPE tokenizer; report proxy vs real side by side; state conditions."}
$12: TEMPLATES:DATA
TMPL:guard_spec{
"tool": "tools/guard.py",
"checks": ["section_layout", "idea_heads", "single_row_tables", "fenced_bloque", "no_col0_braces_in_body", "ascii_identifiers", "content_coverage"],
"inputs": "source.hcortex.md and compiled canonical CORTEX",
"outputs": "guard_report.json with per-document codes, source_ideas, compiled_ideas, coverage",
"pass": "coverage == 1.0 or declared losses; zero silent acceptance",
"fail": "emit specific code and block; never silently accept"
}
TMPL:upstream_issue{
"title": "<defect summary>",
"package": "codec-cortex==1.0.1",
"repro": "minimal vector + exact command",
"expected": "specific diagnostic / preserved content",
"actual": "silent loss / wrong code / missing corpus",
"evidence": "artifact path + sha256",
"impact": "auditability / reproducibility",
"owner_approval": "required before filing PR"
}
TMPL:cell_schema{
"run": "<run-id>",
"cell": "<model>_<format>_<question>_r<k>",
"model": "<declared-id>",
"format": "cortex or json or yaml or markdown or xml or plaintext",
"question": "Q1",
"attempt": 1,
"prompt_sha256": "<64 hex>",
"raw_output": "<verbatim>",
"valid": true,
"diagnostics": [],
"tokens": {"prompt": 0, "completion": 0},
"latency_ms": 0
}
TMPL:acceptance_checklist{
"g1_prereg_frozen": false,
"g2_deterministic_complete": false,
"g3_cells_accounted": false,
"g4_preregistered_stats": false,
"g5_seal_and_claims": false,
"g6_zero_silent_loss": false,
"coverage_eq_1": false,
"fidelity_eq_1": false,
"determinism_eq_1": false,
"tamper_file_eq_1": false,
"error_precision_eq_1_frozen": false,
"h4_h5_verdicts_with_ci": false,
"real_bpe_density": false,
"durable_seal_verifies": false,
"offline_repro_passes": false,
"no_secrets_sealed": false,
"cost_cap_enforced": false
}
TMPL:report_skeleton{
AGENT REMEDIATION REPORT - <run-id>
1. Setup: OS, CPU, Python, package version, tokenizer, model ids and dates.
2. Preregistration: sha256, matrix, R, rubric, exclusion rules.
3. Corpus and baselines: sizes, shapes, provenance, seals.
4. Deterministic properties: fidelity, determinism, density, error precision, tamper, latency, coverage.
5. Comprehension: accuracy per model and format, paired differences with CIs.
6. Generation: validity per model and format, failure modes, token cost.
7. Threats to validity: controls applied and remaining.
8. Limitations and negative results: failed hypotheses with the same prominence.
9. Reproduction: exact commands, including the deterministic-only rerun.
10. Claim table: metric, estimate, CI, n, artifact path, sha256.
}
$13: ACCEPTANCE:CORE
RUL:done_definition{rule:"A fix is done only when its accept criterion is met with sealed evidence and a verifying hash; otherwise its status stays open or blocked.",detail:"Track each FIX f01-f16 against the acceptance_checklist; do not mark done on opinion. Evidence must be reproducible offline."}
TXT:hundred_percent{
100% means the full checklist is green with sealed, durable, hash-traceable evidence:
G1-G6 all pass; coverage=1.0; silent_acceptance_rate=0; fidelity=1.0; determinism=1.0;
tamper_detection(file)=1.0; error_code_precision=1.0 on frozen vectors; H4/H5 completed with verdicts and CIs;
real-BPE density reported; every claim carries path+sha256; offline repro passes; durable seal verifies;
no secrets sealed; cost cap enforced. This is a verifiable definition of done, not a guarantee of model
performance and not a general claim that CORTEX is better. Conditions (model, corpus, prompt, tokenizer)
always accompany any claim.
}
GATE:final{criterion:"All acceptance criteria met with sealed, durable, hash-traceable evidence and owner approval to publish.",evidence:"acceptance_checklist fully true + seal verify log + offline repro log + owner approval"}